      "id": "prose",
      "role": "prose",
      "text": "At the edge of the old bridge, the water carries a record of the hills. Every bend changes the current; every season changes the shore. Looking closely reveals a place that is always moving, even when it appears still. The task of observation is to notice those small changes without hurrying them into a story.",
